~ gatekeeper_look

Unknown: A statue with its hand out. Waiting for something, or someone. [ID:GB_KEEPER_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ gatekeeper_talk

Gatekeeper: Halt. This gate opens only for one who knows the word of the house. [ID:GB_KEEPER_HALT]

=> gatekeeper_ask

~ gatekeeper_ask

Gatekeeper: Speak. [ID:GB_KEEPER_SPEAK]
- What word? [ID:GB_ASK_WORD]
	Gatekeeper: It was carved on the chapel's altar, before the fire. [ID:GB_KEEPER_WORD]
	=> gatekeeper_ask
- Who are you? [if not GameState.get_flag("greybox_asked_who") /] [ID:GB_ASK_WHO]
	do GameState.set_flag("greybox_asked_who")
	Gatekeeper: Stone. I keep the gate. That is all I remember being. [ID:GB_KEEPER_WHO]
	=> gatekeeper_ask
- The word is Mercy. [if GameState.get_flag("greybox_knows_word") /] [ID:GB_SAY_WORD]
	do GameState.set_flag("greybox_word_spoken")
	Gatekeeper: Mercy. Yes. The gate will hear you, if its hinges still can. [ID:GB_KEEPER_HEARD]
	=> END
- Nothing. [ID:GB_LEAVE]
	=> END

~ gate_look

Unknown: Iron, gone orange with rust. Nobody has been through here in a while. [ID:GB_GATE_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ gate_rusted

Unknown: Rusted solid. The hinges haven't moved in years. [ID:GB_GATE_RUSTED_1]

=> END

~ gate_unheard

Unknown: The hinges give a little now. The gate still won't open for me. [ID:GB_GATE_UNHEARD_1]

=> END

~ gate_oiled

Unknown: There. The hinges are drinking it up. [ID:GB_GATE_OILED_1]

=> END

~ gate_opens

Unknown: It gives. Slowly, like it's remembering how. [ID:GB_GATE_OPENS_1]

=> END

~ rag_look_hook

Unknown: A rag on a hook. Somebody's idea of tidy. [ID:GB_RAG_HOOK_1]

=> END

~ rag_take

Unknown: Mine now. Nobody's going to miss it. [ID:GB_RAG_TAKE_1]

=> END

~ rag_look

Unknown: A rag. Dry, stiff, and not much else. [ID:GB_RAG_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ oil_look

Unknown: Lamp oil. Thick, and it still smells of smoke. [ID:GB_OIL_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ oiled_rag_look

Unknown: A rag soaked in oil. Good for a hinge, or a fire. [ID:GB_OILED_RAG_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ altar_look

Unknown: Something was carved here once. The fire took most of it. [ID:GB_ALTAR_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ altar_touch

Unknown: The stone is still warm. Or I am. [ID:GB_ALTAR_TOUCH_1]

=> END

~ altar_past

Unknown: MERCY. Carved deep, before the fire. [ID:GB_ALTAR_PAST_1]

=> END

~ flask_look_shelf

Unknown: A flask on the shelf. Oil, by the smell. [ID:GB_FLASK_SHELF_1]

=> END

~ flask_take

Unknown: Oil. That might help with something rusted. [ID:GB_FLASK_TAKE_1]

=> END

~ window_look

Unknown: Grey light. It doesn't reach the floor. [ID:GB_WINDOW_LOOK_1]

=> END

~ path_look

Unknown: The way on. Whatever is out there, I got this far on my own. [ID:GB_PATH_LOOK_1]

=> END
